  "findings": [
    "7Scenes does not supply a usable SfM point cloud to this pipeline; the prepared reference points are deliberately empty.",
    "The prior nevertheless has real triangulated geometry because the pipeline reconstructs it from mapping RGB at fixed published poses.",
    "High mapping-view PSNR does not certify geometry: Stairs has the best v1 appearance score but the worst v1 reprojection statistics and strong repeated structure.",
    "Only Fire and Stairs have the rectified v4 prior; the other five scenes retain a camera-model disadvantage.",
    "The source-image-free claim applies downstream of the trained Gaussian prior, not to construction of the prior itself."
  ],
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Rebuild chess, heads, office, pumpkin, and redkitchen with the v4 rectified PINHOLE preparation.",
    "Add a mapping-only held-out-trajectory render audit with RGB, depth consistency, reprojection, and valid-mask coverage; do not use test queries for construction or tuning.",
    "Keep geometry evidence and appearance evidence separate; do not use train PSNR as a geometry gate.",
    "Retain semantic-mask absence and 2DGS-specific distortion as explicit limitations when claiming arbitrary-prior compatibility."
  ]
